{
  "sourceLanguage" : "en",
  "strings" : {
    "%@ can speak in a voice that sounds like you, made with Apple's Personal Voice. Choose Ask to Use Personal Voice, then Allow when iOS asks. iOS asks only once." : {

    },
    "%@ can speak in a voice that sounds like you, made with Apple's Personal Voice. iOS asks once whether %@ may use it; choose Allow." : {

    },
    "%@ may use a Personal Voice, but none is on this device. One is made in the Settings app by reading phrases aloud:" : {

    },
    "%@ may use your Personal Voice. It is listed below; Automatic chooses it." : {

    },
    "%@ of normal speed" : {

    },
    "%@ speaks for people who find speaking hard. It keeps what it stores on this device and never sends it to the developer. Copies leave the device only as the privacy policy explains, such as in backups. It has no accounts, no ads and no analytics." : {

    },
    "%@ works with every way an iPhone or iPad can be controlled. Each is part of iOS and is turned on in the Settings app; %@ needs no setup of its own." : {

    },
    "A button on Home already has this name. Choose a different name." : {

    },
    "A partner can point to phrases on the screen for the person to choose with a look, a blink or a nod, then tap the one chosen." : {

    },
    "A simpler iPhone or iPad with only the apps chosen for it. Inside it, %@ fills the screen above the Back button." : {

    },
    "A stray touch or look can leave %@. iOS has two ways to keep someone in it. %@ also keeps the screen from locking while it is open." : {

    },
    "A triple-click of the side or top button (the Home button, on a model that has one) turns chosen features on or off, such as Switch Control or Live Speech. With more than one chosen, a list appears to choose from." : {

    },
    "About %@" : {

    },
    "Accessibility Shortcut" : {

    },
    "Add Switch Control to Settings > Accessibility > Accessibility Shortcut: once it is on, the usual touches cannot turn it off, and a triple-click can." : {

    },
    "Again" : {
      "comment" : "Repeats the last thing spoken."
    },
    "Alert failed" : {

    },
    "Alert stopped" : {

    },
    "Another category already has this name. Choose a different name." : {

    },
    "Answered. iOS asks only once, so any change is made in the Settings app." : {

    },
    "Apple Watch needs watchOS 10 or later." : {

    },
    "Apple's own features for speaking in calls, for Siri, and for running the device with a sound or a button. Each is turned on in the Settings app." : {

    },
    "Ask to Use Personal Voice" : {

    },
    "Assistive Access" : {

    },
    "Assistive Access is on, so these steps are done after leaving it: triple-click the side or top button (the Home button, on a model that has one), choose Exit Assistive Access, and enter its passcode." : {

    },
    "Audio could not start. Speech and Get Attention may be silent. Try again." : {

    },
    "Audio failed" : {

    },
    "Auto Scanning Time sets how fast the highlight moves." : {

    },
    "Auto Tap, under Tap Behavior, taps a selected item after a short wait, without the menu. Pressing the switch again during the wait shows the menu instead." : {

    },
    "Auto-Lock, in Settings > Display & Brightness > Auto-Lock, sets when the screen locks in other apps. While Low Power Mode is on, Auto-Lock is 30 seconds." : {

    },
    "Automatic" : {

    },
    "Back to Talking" : {

    },
    "Calls, Siri and Shortcuts" : {

    },
    "Can't be used while Personal Voice is turned off for %@." : {

    },
    "Check-ins are off. Set Up Step by Step is always here." : {

    },
    "Choose a phrase to speak it." : {
      "comment" : "Shown where the spoken message appears, before anything has been spoken."
    },
    "Choose a picture from the list." : {

    },
    "Choose every way that is used now. Each answer is saved as soon as it is chosen." : {

    },
    "Choose the action. For something Siri does, choose Siri Request and type the request." : {

    },
    "Choose the features a triple-click should reach." : {

    },
    "Choose the other device as the screen shows, then choose Accept on it." : {

    },
    "Choose the voice" : {

    },
    "Choose what it does. With one switch, choose Select Item." : {

    },
    "Choose where the switch is: External, Screen, Camera, Back Tap, Sound or AirPod Gestures." : {

    },
    "Clear" : {
      "comment" : "Empties the typed message. Shown in a category's place while typing."
    },
    "Clear My Choices" : {

    },
    "Connect an external switch first, if one is used. A Bluetooth switch is paired in Settings > Bluetooth." : {

    },
    "Connect the device as its maker explains, and set it up in its own app." : {

    },
    "Couldn't save, so nothing was changed. Try again." : {

    },
    "Create an Assistive Access passcode." : {

    },
    "Device volume is very low. Raise it before relying on speech or Get Attention." : {

    },
    "Done" : {

    },
    "Double-tap the screen with three fingers to zoom in or out, and drag with three fingers to move around." : {

    },
    "During Guided Access, a triple-click reaches them only if Accessibility Shortcut is turned on in Settings > Accessibility > Guided Access. Assistive Access has its own Accessibility Shortcut setting, in Settings > Accessibility > Assistive Access." : {

    },
    "During Guided Access, emergency calls and Crash Detection are not available. Before relying on it, check that Eye Tracking, Switch Control or Voice Control still work with it on this device." : {

    },
    "Dwell Control, on the same screen, chooses a button by looking at it for a moment." : {

    },
    "Earlier setup answers could not be read, so setup starts again. Nothing else was changed." : {

    },
    "Emergency" : {

    },
    "Emergency can't be deleted, so it's always one step away. You can change its phrases." : {

    },
    "Emergency needs at least one phrase. Change this phrase's words instead." : {

    },
    "Enhanced" : {

    },
    "Everything here can be changed later in Family Setup. In about three months, Family Setup will ask whether anything has changed." : {

    },
    "Eye Tracking" : {

    },
    "Eye trackers for iPad" : {

    },
    "Family Setup" : {

    },
    "Family Setup will ask again in 30 days." : {

    },
    "Family Setup will ask again in about three months." : {

    },
    "Family: help with setting up is in Settings." : {

    },
    "First, open Settings > Accessibility > Accessibility Shortcut and make sure Touch Accommodations is selected, so a triple-click can turn it off again if touches stop working as expected." : {

    },
    "Follow the dot with the eyes to calibrate. This happens each time Eye Tracking is turned on." : {

    },
    "For the device's own options, choose Devices, then its name." : {

    },
    "Get Attention" : {

    },
    "Get Attention did not start. Choose it again." : {

    },
    "Get Attention is not sounding. Choose Back until Home appears, then choose Get Attention." : {

    },
    "Get Attention is sounding." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver reads for the status line while the Get Attention alarm sounds."
    },
    "Get Attention stopped unexpectedly. Choose it again to restart." : {

    },
    "Go Through Setup Again" : {

    },
    "Guided Access" : {

    },
    "Guided Access has its own Display Auto-Lock, which sets when the screen locks during a session. Open Settings > Accessibility > Guided Access > Display Auto-Lock and choose the longest time offered." : {

    },
    "Head Tracking" : {

    },
    "Hear" : {

    },
    "Hear %@" : {

    },
    "Hear Automatic" : {

    },
    "Help" : {
      "comment" : "Another name a person can say for the Get Attention control with Voice Control."
    },
    "Helps Siri understand speech that has changed. iOS offers it when the device's language is English (U.S.)." : {

    },
    "Hold Duration sets how long a switch must be held before it counts. Ignore Repeat ignores a press that comes again too soon." : {

    },
    "How is the screen reached?" : {

    },
    "How long a dwell takes is set in Settings > Accessibility > Touch > AssistiveTouch > Dwell Control." : {

    },
    "How long a look takes is set in Settings > Accessibility > Touch > AssistiveTouch > Dwell Control." : {

    },
    "If a triple-click is too fast, a slower click speed is set in Settings > Accessibility > Side Button (Top Button or Home Button on some models)." : {

    },
    "If a triple-click is used to turn features such as Switch Control on or off, turn on Accessibility Shortcut on the same screen, so it still works during Guided Access." : {

    },
    "If three-finger gestures are hard, add Zoom to the Accessibility Shortcut, and turn on Zoom Controller in Zoom's settings." : {

    },
    "In Passcode Settings, set a passcode." : {

    },
    "In Use" : {

    },
    "Keep %@ Open" : {

    },
    "Keeps the iPhone or iPad in one app until a passcode is entered." : {

    },
    "Learn About Each Way" : {

    },
    "Lends the person's accessibility settings to another iPhone or iPad for a while. Sharing ends with Stop Sharing, a triple-click or locking the device, or when the two are more than 30 feet (about 9 m) apart." : {

    },
    "Listen for Atypical Speech" : {

    },
    "Live Speech" : {

    },
    "Live Speech on Apple Watch" : {

    },
    "Live Speech's phrases are its own: %@'s phrases are not in it, so type in the few used most." : {

    },
    "Magnifies the screen." : {

    },
    "Making a Personal Voice means reading phrases aloud, so it is easiest while speaking is comfortable. Apple keeps it encrypted on this device, and in iCloud only if Share Across Devices is on. %@ never receives the voice or its recordings." : {

    },
    "Message" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver calls the field on Home where a message is typed."
    },
    "Message full" : {

    },
    "Message not restored" : {

    },
    "Message not saved" : {

    },
    "More Accessibility Settings" : {

    },
    "Most settings, these guides' steps included, are changed only after leaving Assistive Access." : {

    },
    "Move the pointer by moving the head; choose with a facial expression or Dwell Control." : {

    },
    "Needs can change. Is the screen still reached the same way? Going through setup again takes a few minutes." : {

    },
